  "slug": "cauchy-schwarz-oq-01-oq-04",
  "title": "Formalize Bessel inequality in Hilbert spaces",
  "phase": "DONE",
  "status": "completed",
  "tier": "A",
  "path": "full",
  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "∀ {𝕜 E ι : Type*} [RCLike 𝕜] [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace 𝕜 E] (v : ι → E) (hv : Orthonormal 𝕜 v) (x : E), ∑' i, ‖⟪v i, x⟫_𝕜‖ ^ 2 ≤ ‖x‖ ^ 2",
    "plain": "For any orthonormal family {vᵢ}ᵢ in a Hilbert space E and any vector x, the sum ∑ᵢ |⟨vᵢ,x⟩|² ≤ ‖x‖². When {vᵢ} is a complete orthonormal system (Hilbert basis), equality holds: Parseval's identity.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "Fundamental result in functional analysis connecting orthonormal systems to ℓ²",
      "Generalizes Cauchy-Schwarz from single vectors to orthonormal families",
      "Foundation for Fourier analysis and spectral theory in Hilbert spaces"
    ]
  },
  "knownResults": {
    "proven": [
      "bessel_finite: ∑ᵢ∈s |⟨vᵢ,x⟩|² ≤ ‖x‖² for any finite set s (via Orthonormal.sum_inner_products_le)",
      "bessel_monotone: Bessel sum grows with larger orthonormal sets",
      "bessel_insert: adding one orthonormal vector increases the Bessel sum",
      "bessel_inequality: ∑' i, |⟨vᵢ,x⟩|² ≤ ‖x‖² (infinite case, via tsum_inner_products_le)",
      "bessel_summable: Fourier coefficients are square-summable (via inner_products_summable)",
      "parseval_identity: ∑' i, |⟨bᵢ,x⟩|² = ‖x‖² for HilbertBasis (via lp.norm_rpow_eq_tsum + LinearIsometryEquiv.norm_map)",
      "bessel_extends_cauchy_schwarz: singleton Bessel recovers Cauchy-Schwarz",
      "inner_le_norm: |⟨vᵢ,x⟩| ≤ ‖x‖ from bessel_extends_cauchy_schwarz via nlinarith",
      "bessel_summary: combined statement of finite, infinite, and summability"
    ],
