  "knowledge": {
    "progressSummary": "COMPLETED: Full formalization of Bessel's inequality and Parseval's identity in 199 lines, 11 theorems, 0 axioms, 0 sorries. Key: Mathlib already contains Bessel's inequality as Orthonormal.sum_inner_products_le and tsum_inner_products_le. Parseval uses HilbertBasis.repr_apply_apply + lp.norm_rpow_eq_tsum + LinearIsometryEquiv.norm_map.",
    "builtItems": [
      "CauchySchwarzOQ01OQ04.lean: 199 lines, 11 theorems, 0 axioms, 0 sorries",
      "bessel_finite: directly from Orthonormal.sum_inner_products_le",
      "bessel_inequality: directly from Orthonormal.tsum_inner_products_le",
      "bessel_summable: directly from Orthonormal.inner_products_summable",
      "parseval_identity: HilbertBasis.repr_apply_apply x i = ⟪b i, x⟫ + lp.norm_rpow_eq_tsum + LinearIsometryEquiv.norm_map",
      "inner_le_norm: bessel_extends_cauchy_schwarz (singleton) + nlinarith with sq_nonneg"
    ],
    "insights": [
      "Bessel's inequality is already in Mathlib as Orthonormal.sum_inner_products_le (finite) and tsum_inner_products_le (infinite)",
      "Parseval: HilbertBasis.repr is a LinearIsometryEquiv E ≃ₗᵢ[𝕜] ℓ²(ι,𝕜) with repr_apply_apply x i = ⟪b i, x⟫_𝕜",
      "lp.norm_rpow_eq_tsum converts ‖f‖^p.toReal to ∑' i, ‖f i‖^p.toReal for f ∈ ℓ^p; apply_mod_cast handles the cast",
      "LinearIsometryEquiv.norm_map gives ‖b.repr x‖ = ‖x‖ — the isometry property",
      "Inner product norm bound: |⟨vᵢ,x⟩| ≤ ‖x‖ follows from singleton Bessel via nlinarith [sq_nonneg (‖x‖ - ‖⟪v i, x⟫‖)]",
      "The projection identity ‖x - projₛ x‖² = ‖x‖² - ∑ᵢ∈s |⟨vᵢ,x⟩|² is the algebraic core of Bessel",
      "Monotonicity (bessel_monotone) is Finset.sum_le_sum_of_subset — standard Finset API"
    ],
